                                <div>Hello my name is James Peyroux,</div>
                                <div>
                                    I am a year 11 student from NZ who likes to take walks through the local reserves in Auckland on the weekend. When I created this project my hours which I had been on social media that week according to my phone was 35 hours, 5 hours per day. Surprisingly, this is not a high number with an average of 42 hours in a week for NZ teens.
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    For me, the idea of social media is like the catholic idea of stewardship. We must be able to control ourselves in its usage as we must be able to control ourselves in our actions. Digital wellbeing for nzer’s must be controlled to a point where it does not affect any other aspect of our life.
                                </div>
